                    "latex": "p\\ne0",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ", or ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "q=0",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " and ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "p\\ne0",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p82-q58-b-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The double root is either a nonzero quadratic root or the existing root at zero.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}f(x)&=x(x^2+px+q)\\\\\\Delta&=p^2-4q.\\end{align*}$$\n\nExactly two distinct intercepts requires one double root and one single root.\n\nIf the quadratic has a repeated nonzero root, then $\\Delta=0$, so $p^2=4q$. Its root is $-\\frac{p}{2}$, which must differ from zero. Thus $p\\ne0$, and the distinct roots are $0$ and $-\\frac{p}{2}$.\n\nIf the double root is zero, then $q=0$ and\n$$f(x)=x^2(x+p).$$\nFor $p\\ne0$, the distinct roots are $0$ and $-p$.\n\nTherefore, $p^2=4q$ and $p\\ne0$, or $q=0$ and $p\\ne0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p82-q58-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "three distinct $x$-intercepts.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
